    "sections": {
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"supported%20suitecrm%20versions\">\nSupported SuiteCRM versions\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>SuiteCRM 7.10 onwards. Including SuiteCRM 8.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"how%20is%20the%20data%20exchanged%20with%20suitecrm\">\nHow is the data exchanged with SuiteCRM\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Using the v8 Rest Api introduced in SuiteCRM 7.10.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"what%20is%20needed%20from%20the%20suitecrm%20end\">\nWhat is needed from the SuiteCRM end\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>A user and password of a user, preferrably an administrator user. An oauth client ID and Secret of grant type &#8220;Password&#8221;.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"how%20to%20create%20the%20oauth%20key%20for%20this%20plugin%20in%20suitecrm\">\nHow to create the oauth key for this plugin in suitecrm\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Go to administration page &gt; Users &amp; Authentication block &gt; OAuth2 Clients and Tokens. Click &#8220;New Password Client&#8221;. Enter a name and a secret, and save. And ID is automatically generated and displayed. Note that &#8220;Allowed Grant Type&#8221; will be shown as &#8220;Password Grant&#8221;. The autogenerated ID and the earlier entered secret are what you need to enter in this plugin.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"does%20it%20support%20pulling%20data%20from%20suitecrm%20to%20wordpress\">\nDoes it support pulling data from SuiteCRM to WordPress\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No. Currently only pushing of WordPress users is supported.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial version</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "description": "<p>Send WordPress users to SuiteCRM as contacts, leads, or accounts, automatically or when you choose.</p>\n"
    },
